Extended attributes and RENAME_WHITEOUT for ramfs, which is also tmpfs here (shmem needs an MMU),
both as tmpfs has them: trusted.* and user.* attributes kept in memory with the simple_xattr
helpers, and a rename that leaves a whiteout behind. overlayfs needs the attributes on its upper
layer to make a directory opaque: without them, removing a directory of a lower layer and making
one of the same name failed with EIO (`pip install -U` of a preinstalled package, once the boot
images are laid over the initramfs: engine/src/image_fs.rs, userspace/rootfs/init.c). Without
RENAME_WHITEOUT it only warned at every mount and took two steps for a whiteout.

